remakes and reboots are all the rage  these days in fact they're so popular  that even films from this century  are already getting the refresh  treatment from fantasy films to slasher  flicks these are the remakes of 21st  century films we can expect to see in  the near future with a star-studded cast  including James McAvoy and Tilda Swinton  2005 s The Chronicles of Narnia The Lion  the Witch and the Wardrobe made 745  million dollars worldwide and was one of  the most popular films released that  year it even went on to win a  well-deserved Academy Award for Best  makeup and hairstyling the next  installment was Prince Caspian in 2008  followed by the voyage of the Dawn  Treader in 2010 the film's continued to  be popular but not enough to warrant  another film and the series fourth entry  the Silver Chair was scrapped altogether  however now that game of Thrones is over  there's a great big fantasy shaped whole  for Hollywood to fill so Netflix is  preparing to reboot the Narnia series in  both TV and movie form with 7 books to  adapt and both feature films and series  in the works the streaming service is  about to become a truly magical place it  has holy stuff with its iffy script and  hokey special effects 2011's Green  Lantern was a disaster of heroic  proportions in fact the only positive  anyone can seem to find about Green  Lantern is the film introduced Ryan  Reynolds and Blake Lively who fell in  love on the set and are now married with  three children  DC is bringing the lantern back already  the films working title is Green Lantern  Corps and the screenplay is being  written by DC chief creative officer  Geoff Johns who also wrote Aquaman and  Wonder Woman 1984 Jones is well aware of  the various missteps from the first film  and he's working to make sure those  aren't repeated in his new screenplay  with all their success turning Animated  Classics into live-action films it  should come as no surprise that Disney  has a lilo and Stitch project in the  works lilo and Stitch follows a  rambunctious little Hawaiian girl named  lilo and her caretakers sister Nani  after the death of their parents in a  tragic car accident to help lilo deal  with her grief Nani  her a pet named stitch who turns out to  actually be an alien science project  that escaped to earth filled with  ukulele tunes and lush Hawaiian imagery  lilo and stitch is ultimately a story  about Ohana  ohana means family family means nobody  gets left behind  soon we'll be welcoming a new lilo and  stitch into the Disney family the remake  is being penned by Mike Van ways and  live-action  Aladdin producers Dan Lin and Jonathan  eirick will be overseeing production no  casting information is available yet but  hopefully the cast will reflect Lee  Lowe's home of kawaii and feature lots  of Native Hawaiian representation the  hit Pirates of the Caribbean franchise  may have worn out its welcome by the  fifth film but that hasn't stopped  Disney from pushing ahead with a remake  with a fresh new cast deadpool writers  Rhett Reese and Paul Wernick had been on  deck to write a screenplay that would  bring an edgier twist to the franchise  however both writers jumped ship in  February 2009 teen leaving the project  without a captain or rudder for a while  the future of the project seemed  uncertain but in late 2019 Disney  brought on Chernobyl creator Craig Mazin  and former pirate scribe Ted Elliott to  craft the screenplay leaving the future  of the franchise looking bright for a  moment there it looked like the Resident  Evil franchise was coming to an end with  the final chapter in 2016 but two years  later a new reboot was already in the  works the news broke during Cannes Film  Festival 2018 when it was announced that  47 meters down director johannes roberts  would write and direct the new film  screenwriter greg russo has already  written a screenplay but we're not sure  if roberts is revising Bruce's version  or starting from scratch as for Resident  Evil star Emilio Vova CH she's been  vocal about her displeasure with the  news voicing suspicions that the  producers are doing this just for money  and not for love of the game or the fans  sounds like there may be some bad zombie  blood behind the scenes Shrek was a  global phenomenon that spawned several  equally loved sequels and television  specials as well as multiple spin-offs  it may seem almost sacrilegious to  reboot the 2001 film but upcoming writer  and director Chris melody andriy has  said when you look back on those vocal  performances from the original they're  awesome and while you certainly could  make a case for a complete reinvention  I find myself responding to my own  nostalgic feelings of wanting to go back  to those characterizations melody andriy  has said he'd be interested in bringing  back the original cast which makes the  next Shrek film sound like more sequel  than reboot  however he has also said that it's been  challenging finding a story that doesn't  feel like just another sequel and that  the story he's working on is entirely  new leaving us unsure of exactly what  form the new Shrek will take DreamWorks  2011 animated comedy Puss in Boots  followed Puss and his pre shrek  adventures and was so successful that it  was subsequently adapted into the  television show The Adventures of Puss  in Boots produced by Netflix but if you  still can't get enough of Katt swinging  swords then prepare for another  adventure since a reboot is coming soon  Despicable Me creator and illumination  entertainment founder Chris Smelley Don  dree told variety he's working on an  entirely new story for the swashbuckling  feline we don't have any details on the  plot yet but melody Andriy says he  wouldn't be averse to having the old  cast returned for the remake  eunsung hos heart-stopping south korean  zombie film train to Busan was an  instant classic and a tall order to  remake but if anyone's up to the  challenge its James Wan the harrowing  story follows a father and his young  daughter who find themselves trapped on  a train at the beginning of a zombie  apocalypse between the tender story that  unfolds between the father and daughter  and endearing performances from the  supporting cast trained to busan's  ability to balance its high-concept  premise with the humanity of its  characters helped it achieve both  critical and financial success after an  extensive bidding war new line will be  the studio behind James wons  english-language remake written by his  longtime Annabel collaborator Gary  Doberman while there's no casting or  other news available yet about the  remake the upcoming sequel to the  original film train to Busan - peninsula  can help pass the time check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about your favorite  stuff are coming soon subscribe to our  YouTube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

